  <learnings>["Measurement beat design on a question that looked like a design question. Arky's retention ruling was well-argued and correct in conclusion, but the measurement pass showed the property under protection was never at risk — states/ is a cache the restore path never reads. Measure the artifact before designing a policy for it.", "When two agents contradict each other, resolve rather than average or defer. Arky said contentId is an unsafe dedup key (57% multi-body); measurement said codeEssence is 100% invariant per contentId. Both true at different scopes, and only the explicit reconciliation makes the 19.6x fix legal — deferring would have preserved a true-but-misapplied objection as a blocker.", "The most valuable output of an observability design pass was a demonstration, not a design: hook install succeeds, commit succeeds, no fabric is created, status reports clean. A reproduction reorders a priority list in a way that no amount of argument does.", "Check whether the instrument already exists before building it. oracle.ts already computed the exact meaning-vs-git confusion matrix; the gap was that shadow.ts never calls mergeTree and oracle.jsonl has zero readers. The unanswerable-retroactively item turned out to be wiring, not construction.", "Per-seal cost being independent of changed files is the kind of fact that only falls out of a controlled experiment — a 1-file and a 20-file seal produced identical deltas. It inverts the intuition that a VCS charges for what changed, and it is what makes the curve linear in project SIZE rather than in activity."]</learnings>
